# Build intermediates.
# Directory.Build.props sends them outside the mod folder: they must never end up back inside,
# since the whole folder is uploaded to the Workshop as-is.
.build/
Source/obj/
Source/bin/

# Agent worktrees. The repository root already ignores these, but that .gitignore does not
# survive `git subtree split` - the published repository would start with no rule at all.
#
# And git is only half of it: SteamUGC.SetItemContent takes the junction's target directory as
# it stands on disk, with no filtering and no knowledge of .gitignore. A worktree dropped in a
# mod folder ships to every subscriber however thoroughly git ignores it. MintchocoConfectionery
# reached 210 MB that way, 206 MB of it a .claude worktree.
#
# The rule below is the second line of defence. The first is that only Mod/ is published and
# the RimWorld junction points at Mod/, never at this directory.
.claude/

# Development environments
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.csproj.user

# System
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
